WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.200
Subtitles by [SubsWhen] (https://anidex.info/user/20225)

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.160
- Warning audio?
- Yeah.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.700
If you accidentally played a CD-ROM of
SEGA Saturn with something like a boombox...

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:11.500
You may risk damaging the speakers.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:16.040
In order to prevent that, some disks
contained a warning message.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:18.590
It's fun finding a disk like that and listening to the message.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.550
Hm? Where's the CD boombox...?

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.930
We don't have a CD player here.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.590
That said, neither do I.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:29.890
Huh!? Do young people nowadays not listen to warning messages anymore...?

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:33.730
Were warning messages such a big deal back then?

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.940
Was there nothing else better to listen to?

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.140
Refrain　消した記憶

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.140
​Refrain from those lost memories

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:58.430
Rely on the words from those ordinary stories

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.650
Don't end this  Won't change it

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.650
Don't end this. Won't change it​.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:03.310
Nothing's gonna make a difference

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.690
Don't ever lose sight of your goal​

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.400
Who was the one to decide?

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:14.830
That way of life is unlike you

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:18.080
Having the strength to pursue your goal

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.330
That's what it means to be strong​

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:24.710
It's something you already knew

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.880
I believe in what I've done

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.010
No reason to go back again

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:33.720
Those days gone by full of precious moments

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.600
Easy losing memories

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.720
I'm struggling now to overcome

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:42.400
I'm never going to give up​ until the very end​

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.270
Get down Let's get down

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.270
Get down. Let's get down.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:51.150
The light still shines in my heart

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.820
Trust yourself

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.910
Don't be naive

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:58.120
Save yourself

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.580
Don't forget

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:08.280
Oh no no no no no.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.410
This is a game disk of the SEGA Saturn.

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:12.450
So you don't have to use a boombox...

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.500
You can listen to it directly on the Saturn!?

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.370
If only you had the Internet back in your days, Uncle.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:20.380
Is it that dangerous to put it in a boombox?

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.880
Ah, yeah.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.090
If you press fast-forward by mistake...

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:27.220
You'll get a loud noise like that.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:28.470
Note: "<i>Striker 1945</i>", a vertical-scrolling shooter game published by the Japanese developer Psikyo in 1995.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.430
So you did that before.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:31.680
Speaking of CDs, have I told you about the Singing Monster?

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:32.760
Huh, what's that?

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.600
Were there monsters like that?

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.180
Ah, could you even call that a monster...

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:38.560
Well, you'll know it when you see it.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.310
Icuras Elran

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:44.280
This was about a month or so after what happened at the hot springs.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:47.650
I took on a quest from a town to slay a Singing Monster.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:49.240
Here I was heading into the woods.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:51.780
♪ <i>Dold of Knowledge</i> ♪

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.660
Wh— That's huge!

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:51.780
What's that!?

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:55.740
♪ <i>Shaleg of Form</i> ♪

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:01.040
♪ <i>Jato of Mystery</i> ♪

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:05.170
♪ <i>Head on to the shrines</i> ♪

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.050
It really is singing.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:14.430
♪ <i>Passing the trials of the three shrines</i> ♪

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:09.720
Is that a song from Granbahamal?

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:22.810
♪ <i>A foreign warrior guided by God</i> ♪

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:18.060
Regsuuld Zaldohna

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:21.230
Kilaidor Urgo Riouran

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:36.620
Ice?

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.870
W-Wolfgunblood?

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:45.630
So, the Singing Monster... It was you, Mabel.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.590
And you were singing just now...

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.840
You heard!?

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.880
N-No... Not that!

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:54.640
What are you doing out here in the woods?

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.970
You'll get attacked by monsters.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.850
It's fine.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:02.980
The Beast Robe is enchanted with illusion magic after all.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:04.360
Look!

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:08.860
Amazing! Cute! Let me keep you!

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:08.860
S-Stop petting me!

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:15.450
W-With this, I could be camping anywhere I want without worrying about monsters.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.870
Hm? Camping?

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:21.540
Don't you have a stable job as a knight in the capital?

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.210
You don't see the big picture, huh?

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:30.090
Huh!? Mabel-san, don't tell me...

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.550
You gave up such a good...

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:35.430
Well, it's who I am.

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:39.010
The skies over the capital feels so constraining...

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:41.390
For me.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:44.560
What a free way of life.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.560
She overdid it.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:47.310
Why's Mabel-san always proping herself up like that?

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:53.240
Well, just like that, I'm now living a self-sufficient life here in the woods.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.280
No one would dare to approach if I put up this scary ice sculpture.

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:59.490
I'm gonna stay here forever!

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.120
Is that so? Then...

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:02.830
I'll defeat you.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.670
Eh? Wh-Wh-Wh...

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:09.630
I took on a quest from the town of Jato to slay a Singing Monster.

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:13.470
If Mabel, the true identity of the Monster, isn't willing to leave...

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:15.010
Defeating you is the only...

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.840
I-I get it! I'll leave!

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:17.800
Huh?

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.520
I... see...

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.020
O... Okay.

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:25.940
He was disappointed for a split second!

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:28.310
Was he still thinking about defeating Mabel-san?

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:34.740
Goodbye to this place too, huh?

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.950
What am I gonna do tomorrow?

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.830
Hm? That's easy.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:41.620
Just sell the ring I gave you before.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.040
Ah, have you sold it already?

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.050
Oh, so you still have it.

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:58.050
Well, you should sell it in town tomorrow.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.060
I'm keeping this, so no way!

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:04.810
So you're the type who's not willing to use a single bomb even if it means a game over.

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:06.640
I feel you.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:11.730
Then, how about making money as a bard or something...?

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.070
Since you're a good singer.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:15.530
I-I'm not that good!

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:19.410
Your singing back there... I don't think it's something that can be achieved in a single day or two.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:25.790
Th-That's because I've always been singing by myself.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:28.120
Doing it in front of others is kind of...

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:32.960
Ah, it's nice doing something by yourself, I get it.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.180
But it's a shame.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:42.510
You're cute, and you sing well...

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:45.810
Ah, you did that again...

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:47.390
Wolf, you're always like this...

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:51.360
If you were in Japan's entertainment industry, you'd be hella rich for life.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:55.940
Huh? Hella rich?

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:58.360
Life in Japanbahamal is so damn easy!

00:06:58.450 --> 00:06:59.490
Wait, for life!?

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:01.530
Filthy rich.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:06.540
Damn, that's awesome! The otherworld sounds great! I wanna go there!

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:08.080
That's right.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.500
How am I gonna go back?

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:22.260
- Wh-What if...
- Hm?

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:25.510
I mean, if you don't mind...

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:29.850
I could sing for you the songs from your home.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:35.230
Are you sure? I thought you don't like to sing in front of people...

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:37.530
Because...

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:40.740
You looked so lonely!

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:45.530
Th-This is all... I can do.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:49.580
Thank you. You're so kind.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:53.250
I-I'm not very good at it, but if you teach me, I'll do my best!

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:54.380
So...

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:57.590
We practiced for a bit. Let me fast-forward.

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:59.470
S-Say Uncle...

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.130
What kind of songs do you listen to?

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:03.840
This here is something both of you should know.

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:06.260
After all, it's composed by a pretty famous musician.

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:07.180
- Huh?
- Who?

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:08.350
Let's see...

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.180
Okay, right here.

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:50.430
Ah!? Shopping mall!?

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:51.730
Vacation...?

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:53.730
See? You've heard it before.

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:55.730
I was there when I was a kid...

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:58.440
The UFO Catcher in the state-of-the-art game center!

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:58.440
The UFO Catcher in the rundown game center!

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:04.530
It was originally a BGM for "<i>Sonic the Hedgehog</i>".

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:04.530
Note: BGM for the Star Light Zone.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:06.410
See? It's about SEGA after all!

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:08.620
Its composer is that well-known...

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:08.620
Note: Masato Nakamura, a Japanese musician and record producer.

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.240
No, that's fine.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:11.950
We wouldn't know even if you tell us.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:13.370
Yeah?

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:18.960
H-How was it? Wolf...

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:20.170
Huh?

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:32.770
You'll go back to your world someday, huh?

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:36.190
I wish I could go too... Wolf's home...

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:38.440
That mysterious world.

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:41.400
♪ <i>In a dream I could see</i> ♪

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.150
♪ <i>You are not far away</i> ♪

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:51.790
♪ <i>Anytime anyplace, I can see your face</i> ♪

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.320
Uncle, what's this song?

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:50.160
Note: "Nights into Dreams", a 1996 game published by SEGA for the SEGA Saturn.

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:50.160
This is the ending song from "<i>NiGHTS</i>".

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.580
Should've let her sing it first...

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:57.120
♪ <i>You're that special one that I have been waiting for</i> ♪

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:58.460
If we follow Mabel Rayveil the bait, we're sure to find that dragon-shifting orc.

00:09:57.180 --> 00:10:03.840
♪ <i>And I hope you're looking for someone like me</i> ♪

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.210
Just as Commander Markfeld predicted.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:01.630
Ah, these guys...

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:05.090
The Royal Knights!

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:09.800
♪ <i>In my dreams, I can hear you calling me</i> ♪

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:07.260
Were they going after Uncle?

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:10.050
All right, let's go. While he's sleeping...

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:13.550
♪ <i>In the night</i> ♪

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:13.140
W-Who goes there!? Hey, stop!

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:16.230
♪ <i>Everything's so sweet</i> ♪

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:21.900
♪ <i>In your eyes I feel</i> ♪

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:29.700
♪ <i>There's so much inside</i> ♪

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:35.330
♪ <i>In the nights, dream delight</i> ♪

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:36.750
So the Elf came to the rescue.

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:43.050
♪ <i>I want to see you standing there</i> ♪

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:41.880
She's got a nice side after all.

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:43.300
It's totally gonna be carnage!

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:48.380
♪ <i>In the nights, dream delight</i> ♪

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:46.090
This is nothing to ha-ha-ha about...!

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:48.010
S-She's st-staring...!

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:49.220
Scary!!

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.760
♪ <i>I've found someone...</i> ♪

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:51.140
Well, you get the idea.

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:55.100
U-Uncle, so you like game music then?

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:56.850
Sure do.

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:58.480
Icuras Elran

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:03.020
I especially like the tracks from "Dynamite Headdy".

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:06.280
Alright, let's give them a listen.

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:12.990
What's wrong, Uncle?

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:19.500
I've always thought that the heroine of "Dynamite Headdy" was called "Fingy"...

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:22.830
But it's actually "Fingi" with a short "i"!!

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:24.130
Oh...

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:25.420
I see...

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:30.840
Uncle?

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.480
Funky monkey uncley! It's the Uncle again, comin' atcha!

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:48.900
Hi everyone, welcome to the channel, Uncle from Another World...

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:53.450
U... Uncle from Another World...

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:55.910
What am I even doing?

00:11:55.990 --> 00:12:00.580
I've mistaken "Fingi" for "Fingy" for over a decade...

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:02.960
Incorrect Uncle, that's who I am.

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:04.460
Hey! Cut! Cut!

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:05.840
Let's just call it a day!

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:10.300
The boss in the fifth stage is Madam Barber. Her human form is Onigoroshi Kyouko.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:14.850
A Long-distance dump truck driver and a strong mother.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:14.850
Simply getting the names wrong isn't that much of a big deal.

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:15.760
I know, right?

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:19.470
No, names are important. It's what she said.

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:20.770
Who's she?

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:21.890
The Elf.

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.690
It was the day after Mabel sang for me...

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:26.900
...when she told me her real name.

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.530
Let's see, next up is...

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:31.740
Show us!

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:32.820
But the manual, I haven't...

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:34.490
Show us, Uncle!!

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:42.830
You look happy, orc-face.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:44.620
Oh, it's you.

00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:46.960
I thought I've managed to lose you.

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:48.040
What's that?

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:51.760
‪Are two of you singing and living together? Here? Forever?

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:54.760
Or are you going to make out with the Hero in the bath again?

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:57.180
What are you on about? Mabel and Alicia, they're...

00:12:57.260 --> 00:12:59.220
Ah, yes. Here it is again.

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:02.020
Mabel, Mabel, Alicia, Alicia.

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:06.020
What's with you, calling them by their names all the time?

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:08.820
I've known you for much longer than they do.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.030
Oh no!

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.030
You didn't say my name once...

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:11.440
Your name...

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:13.610
You've never told me your name in the first place.

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:15.410
Is that it? Is "Elga" fine with you?

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:17.870
- That's my clan name, stupid!
- Stu...

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:23.410
Haven't you been calling me "stupid" or "orc" or whatever you want?

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:26.170
Huh!? That's because you never tell anyone your real name!

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.580
It's Shibazaki Yousuke.

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:29.000
Huh!? Shiba—

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:35.880
Eh? Shibazaki of the Yousuke clan?

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:38.090
It's Yousuke of the Shibazaki clan.

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:42.970
H-How do you write it? How do you write it?

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:44.100
Write it?

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:53.940
Shibazaki means "island's cape".

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:58.320
Yousuke means something like "helping others with joy".

00:13:58.410 --> 00:14:00.450
Yo-u-su...

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:02.910
This is "Yo"...

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:04.080
"u"

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:05.620
"su"

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:07.870
Yousuke.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:19.510
W-Why are you telling me this all of a sudden?

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:22.850
I didn't think stuff like my real name would interest you.

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:25.810
It's not just "stuff"! Names are important!

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:27.560
You're right.

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:29.150
What about yours?

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.150
I told you my name already.

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:36.610
I... I'm...

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:41.410
Suzailgiererzegalnelvzegilreagranzelga Elga.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:50.460
Suzailgiererzegalnelvzegilreagranzelga Elga!

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:54.380
Suza-i...

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:57.880
I can't remember a name that long.

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:01.050
So, just call me Elf.

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:02.640
How about "Sui"?

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:04.310
As a nickname. Then...

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:06.390
The name of royalty...

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:08.350
Shortening it is disrespectful to the authority...

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:10.650
You don't like this nickname?

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:12.310
Then I'll go Elf just as before.

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:14.900
It's not a problem of whether I like it or not!

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:19.650
I mean, my clan... my nation... they won't allow it!

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:23.620
I'm asking you personally if you like it.

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:28.620
"Sui" means "green" in the Japanbahamal language.

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:32.580
"Hisui" is a word for the green gemstone, jade.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:35.880
Sui...

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:41.470
I came up with this nickname when I saw your beautiful, jewel-like eyes.

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:45.640
Wait... no way, jewels...?

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:47.430
Oh, you don't like it? Then Elf it is...

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:50.310
-Yousuke!
- What is it, Sui?

00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:53.480
N-No, d-d-d-don't call me that!

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.230
Oh, then I won't.

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:56.940
Stupid Yousuke!

00:15:57.530 --> 00:16:00.860
What I mean is you can't call me that in front of other people.

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:02.910
And I won't say your name either.

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:04.660
Not even mine? Why?

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:07.870
B-Because only I can...

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:09.620
Explain yourself, Sui.

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:12.920
J-Just because!

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.220
Well, here's how it went.

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:22.220
U-Uncle!

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:24.180
That's amazing!

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:29.350
Wolf! What do we eat?

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.560
It's Elf!

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:33.560
It's been a long time, Mabel.

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:35.900
Ah, your ring!

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:40.990
Hm? Huh? What?

00:16:41.070 --> 00:16:43.910
S-So what are you two doing here?

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:49.700
I was curious about those ruins so I was just walking to check them out.

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.670
This is the shrine of Jato.

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:56.710
Is that the one you were singing about yesterday?

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:58.380
Icuras Elran

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:07.600
♪ <i>Passing the trials of the three shrines</i> ♪

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:02.590
My voice? What's that spell?

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:05.640
Is this desolate building one of the "three shrines"?

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:15.440
♪ <i>A foreign warrior guided by God</i> ♪

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:09.350
No one even maintained it!?

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:11.470
Well, even if it's destroyed...

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:15.440
It only carries meaning to the foreign warrior.

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:17.810
- Foreign...
- Warrior...

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:20.320
If it's orc-face...

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:22.400
Couldn't he take on the trials of the shrines?

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:24.490
Baraibuuto Forugu Basutooru

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:51.310
The Great Raging Power of God.

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:54.140
I'll go for maximum firepower from the get-go!

00:17:54.230 --> 00:17:56.100
Kilaido Rugido Riolan

00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:58.060
Kuroo Rugido Riolan

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:01.020
No, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait...

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:03.150
...wait, wait, wait, wait, wait. S-Stop, Uncle!

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:05.860
Destroying the shrine's gonna bring about disasters!

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:07.570
Huh!? That's exactly why I destroyed it.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:08.740
You did that on purpose!?

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:12.290
It was some great power that brought me to the otherworld.

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:16.830
If I defeat the great power of the shrine, then maybe...

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:18.830
I'd make some progress.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:23.460
Uncle, do you know nothing except for defeating the enemies to move forward?

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:25.550
You're too carefree about this.

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:29.340
Wait, how come this happened when you've destroyed only one shrine?

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:31.810
There were three of them...

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:35.640
The memory spirit is doing something...

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:36.640
This is...

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:40.520
That time when Alicia's party and you defeated the goblin army...

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.610
Dold

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:42.730
Shaleg

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:45.530
It was you, Uncle!

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:48.610
Uncle, you destroyed the other shrines too!

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:50.030
So it was me.

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:54.330
It'd be nice if there's an on-screen notification showing that you've destroyed a shrine.

00:18:54.410 --> 00:18:55.750
It's not a game...

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:56.910
This is bad.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:58.920
Well, let's continue.

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:08.130
No effect!?

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:09.300
No...

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:11.850
The grass...!

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:14.560
This abnormal burst of life...

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:17.230
That's a lump of holy magic.

00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:19.770
It doesn't have a physical body, so the attacks are ineffective!

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:23.060
Holy magic does things like healing, right?

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:31.030
The dead monsters around here... They're recovering and going out of control!

00:19:32.870 --> 00:19:34.660
Long Heavy Piercer!

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:42.080
Suffocate by my icy blade and go to sleep!

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:53.260
There's no end to this!

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:56.220
Then I'll turn it to ash up close!!

00:19:56.810 --> 00:19:58.890
Baraibut Folg

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:08.280
Wolf?

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:11.610
Bustor

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:33.010
Not bad, Mabel Rayveil.

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:36.050
Never thought I'll be the one being protected.

00:20:36.140 --> 00:20:39.390
T-The God-Freezing Sword isn't just for show...

00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:41.940
B-But why'd Wolf...?

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:46.650
There's a type of holy magic that lets you manipulate others with mind control.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:48.150
That's probably the reason.

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:49.110
Oh crap!

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:53.860
Shura Breaker!

00:20:56.780 --> 00:20:58.700
Okay, that's one orc down!

00:20:58.790 --> 00:20:59.620
All you two all right?

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:04.580
We're here to slay the Singing Monster!

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:05.920
Let us handle the rest...

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:07.840
Alicia-dono!?

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:09.550
Huh, who?

00:21:11.840 --> 00:21:13.760
H-Here it comes...

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:15.720
The three of them got together!

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:17.180
Big sis Elf!?

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:19.760
…Huh!? Then that orc is...

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:24.190
Kuroki! I'm sorry, I'll heal you right now...!

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:25.440
Wait!

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:27.770
Orc-face is under mind control, he's dangerous!

00:21:28.940 --> 00:21:31.110
We're not fighting the Singing Monster here...

00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:33.740
Our enemy's the lump of holy magic that has been let loose.

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:38.530
B-Body manipulation...

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:40.910
I'll get him back with the power of the wand!

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:43.870
No! The Power of God is too strong!

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:47.080
Let the inner waves of the mind led astray...

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:49.130
Be united with my own!

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:10.650
Kuroki.

00:22:12.690 --> 00:22:14.190
Alicia, are you okay!?

00:22:14.280 --> 00:22:16.030
Geez, I told you so!

00:22:16.110 --> 00:22:19.660
K... Kuroki's past memories...

00:22:19.740 --> 00:22:21.660
I made contact with the darkness inside of him.

00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:23.580
The darkness inside?

00:22:24.660 --> 00:22:26.620
Kuroki, as a child...

00:22:26.710 --> 00:22:31.460
He lived in a tiny room with nothing but a cold, black box before him.

00:22:31.540 --> 00:22:33.340
Orc-face had such a dark...

00:22:33.420 --> 00:22:35.210
- That's awful.
- I feel sorry.

00:22:35.300 --> 00:22:36.840
I didn't realize...

00:22:36.920 --> 00:22:41.680
That amount of darkness is beyond my power...

00:22:36.920 --> 00:22:41.680
Could you not oversimply my past as just some darkness...?

00:22:43.890 --> 00:22:45.980
Something you don't understand...

00:22:47.850 --> 00:22:50.230
Something you don't even try to understand.

00:22:50.860 --> 00:22:55.030
Forcing your values upon others...

00:22:55.740 --> 00:22:57.030
Stop it.

00:22:58.110 --> 00:23:04.290
Don't force me to play soccer with the soccer club during class!

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:01.490
I-Isn't he under mind control...?

00:23:01.570 --> 00:23:03.120
He's speaking...!

00:23:03.200 --> 00:23:04.290
Scary...!

00:23:04.370 --> 00:23:07.250
Reguuld Stagga

00:23:08.460 --> 00:23:10.170
Stagga Magna

00:23:15.840 --> 00:23:17.420
Waagurendo Gurakka

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:22.390
That bottle...

00:23:22.470 --> 00:23:23.970
Where have I...?

00:23:39.320 --> 00:23:40.700
Blaze...

00:23:40.780 --> 00:23:42.200
Dragon...?

00:23:42.740 --> 00:23:44.990
Orc-face! Don't tell me...!?

00:23:45.080 --> 00:23:46.120
Yeah.

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:50.160
I'm not gonna fight something with no physical body.

00:23:50.250 --> 00:23:52.000
Blaze Dragon...

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:54.590
With its Power of God...

00:23:54.670 --> 00:23:57.460
Let it absorb all the healing energy...

00:23:57.550 --> 00:23:59.260
And I'll defeat it!!
